[{"id":"VRCE-6-23-1","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":23,"verse":1,"english":"Seeing that head and that excellent bow, and (remembering) the union of (Rama) and Sugriva related by Hanumãn, and (seeing) those eyes, and the complexion of that face, and that countenance like to that of her lord, and that hair and that forehead; and that beautiful jewel forming the crest; and recognizing (Rāma) by all these tokens combined, (Sītā), exceedingly aggrieved, rebuked Kaikeyī, lamenting like a female osprey.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-32-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6023001","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2c2b57ed60a64e78ec4ce27e302af8a00ac4817251ec006a48ed9bbd9544e9d8","compact":"3e14e81835016298835d7176c1919cc4e4f115725ab5dbd6abd2d8760a094e45","nasal":"3e14e81835016298835d7176c1919cc4e4f115725ab5dbd6abd2d8760a094e45"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-23-2","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":23,"verse":2,"english":"Seeing that head and that excellent bow, and (remembering) the union of (Rama) and Sugriva related by Hanumãn, and (seeing) those eyes, and the complexion of that face, and that countenance like to that of her lord, and that hair and that forehead; and that beautiful jewel forming the crest; and recognizing (Rāma) by all these tokens combined, (Sītā), exceedingly aggrieved, rebuked Kaikeyī, lamenting like a female osprey.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-32-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6023002","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"590112ded86314f30e76886416cc3cdcfa19bc84325878c2d6d24e64017a108a","compact":"3be97cae1e9118bc5dd54206a0a5587b47ed24028f46d77d7d048b1aacd4734b","nasal":"98008bf22cf8a8eebbab3fd819992e7876a9428df9671ee5e65a61f0d16016dd"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-23-3","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":23,"verse":3,"english":"Seeing that head and that excellent bow, and (remembering) the union of (Rama) and Sugriva related by Hanumãn, and (seeing) those eyes, and the complexion of that face, and that countenance like to that of her lord, and that hair and that forehead; and that beautiful jewel forming the crest; and recognizing (Rāma) by all these tokens combined, (Sītā), exceedingly aggrieved, rebuked Kaikeyī, lamenting like a female osprey.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.705,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-32-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6023003","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ea54ff9144146511c00bbab8c7606bc595b212414ae7409c2d6ebc16c84aa11e","compact":"3a282ddc277ed0abc89c6e3fb1d36121a095509271380298350ef42c4ce8df48","nasal":"029972c087bb704877749d01304c1ea3aafe07833f01be022eb9bc3ca30e83d0"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-23-4","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":23,"verse":4,"english":"O Kaikeyſ, have your wishes attained. Slain has been the son of the race; and the entire race is exterminated by you, partial to dissension.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-32-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6023004","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"57f0c917b4d9a8ec5b02eebe293ef20254e77b56ba83f1c4e1f95c54a2629c8b","compact":"1ac047628ab9cdffca0f68a765d079f9f0732b81951f5ba9353172e81203e8d4","nasal":"69f2d32dab9d75bce9183e436cf9107fdaec7bd2d3352ed3caddd693093cdbcb"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-23-5","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":23,"verse":5,"english":"What evil had been done to Kaikeyi by the revered Rāma, that along with me, he had been banished into the woods, with rags given him (for his covering)?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.485,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-32-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6023005","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8aa21eda7d116051f72f07a8018ffa8c6112229095a029bdc9a3699342360b97","compact":"83fdd072254d2ee32a27006ce6b4c68573ec329906cf1513b161ee297145d95f","nasal":"83fdd072254d2ee32a27006ce6b4c68573ec329906cf1513b161ee297145d95f"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-23-6","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":23,"verse":6,"english":"Having said this, Vaidehi, forlorm and trembling (all over), dropped to the earth, like a plantain cut off.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-32-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6023006","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"01ccbcd2efa2d150d0718c57158fd6114fbb8da58299842bc565ebd4908ed3b2","compact":"efa9d83b59ffe52c74deecbf5e8fa36662f7c32698ae786fcb036ca6f3980a58","nasal":"54d1a3f555a5ae92e8755cc7ba7efd06fbc44fccb520f2cfc94ccea33371c603"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-23-7","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":23,"verse":7,"english":"Then, recovering after a while, and having regained her consciousness, the large-eyed one, placing the head in her front, gave way to grief.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.476,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-32-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6023007","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f1e7240e32023e231d92288c44613ddc867f6a2290e4eb90430191d3a6b31752","compact":"2e59c1c74a546fdc740bb297b51c14261fe1181a5785904bdcd03f9dc739ae46","nasal":"2e59c1c74a546fdc740bb297b51c14261fe1181a5785904bdcd03f9dc739ae46"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-23-8","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":23,"verse":8,"english":"Ah! I am undone, O mighty-armed one! ) you that did follow stern vows! From your (death), I have come by this final plight, having been rendered a widow.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.864,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-32-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6023008","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"015bea381784fae71aabe8e2e95c1f6617c7c2f2eb0cfee4aa273a8aa15d9482","compact":"39df2520db38d13c55f4d2f63c5eff688232415f62021e895acacfc5c368fd1e","nasal":"39df2520db38d13c55f4d2f63c5eff688232415f62021e895acacfc5c368fd1e"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-23-9","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":23,"verse":9,"english":"The greatest calamity (that can befall a woman), is said to be the death of her husband. And, possessor of an excellent character, you have departed before me, who have ever trod the path of the righteous; but who have come by a mighty grief and am plunged in a sea of sorrow.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-32-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6023009","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5c979a453c0f3807c3190034553852a981da022da507b9c2eefa81e4b6fc05f5","compact":"b58ff2fd0ba3a8147e723e05d56f5b9873c68c003f19869e47ee102f6f1bf24c","nasal":"b58ff2fd0ba3a8147e723e05d56f5b9873c68c003f19869e47ee102f6f1bf24c"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-23-10","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":23,"verse":10,"english":"The greatest calamity (that can befall a woman), is said to be the death of her husband. And, possessor of an excellent character, you have departed before me, who have ever trod the path of the righteous; but who have come by a mighty grief and am plunged in a sea of sorrow. And you, who was engaged in delivering me, have yourself fallen! And my mother-in-law, Kausalyā, attached (to you), through the death of you, her son, at the hands of Raksasas, has been reduced to the condition of a cow that has been deprived of her calf.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.457,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-32-7","DUTT-6-32-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6023010","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6a96a2fe8f8ea1ad4449d84648319d7dea85462551918a255b68d0da17f471da","compact":"3acf027ce15e7af04d80125d427a41cf1d4823af84f3b12abb4282eb06b7463c","nasal":"ffe6d7452168d6b5585847d8ca16dde3326d233207e67f2579ce6dd5cad0065f"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-23-11","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":23,"verse":11,"english":"And you, who was engaged in delivering me, have yourself fallen! And my mother-in-law, Kausalyā, attached (to you), through the death of you, her son, at the hands of Raksasas, has been reduced to the condition of a cow that has been deprived of her calf.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.825,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-32-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6023011","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1f0be56fafa711cb06c8accb55e18e2848d9f115aac46bb7bd66df2dd8dc2c6e","compact":"b24328f3bd5725243366dd8085d3e380ceffb5973d745513a4e04878e0332aaa","nasal":"b24328f3bd5725243366dd8085d3e380ceffb5973d745513a4e04878e0332aaa"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-23-12","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":23,"verse":12,"english":"O Rāghava, even the astrologers had predicted long life for you. But their words are false, you, O Rāghava, wast short-lived. me","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.421,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-32-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6023012","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6539e2209e6c97877433b8e080eca67eaf0f14423fb9794f9bf41cb09db81bea","compact":"3ea2e7013a8567d6dd98b4f94cfe98205727501b5f1b8f6b2766b485d7c8826e","nasal":"a6f65771ccb3b786ffbcd99d405fdf5e5112701c4f76f2c5feceb773d03d2312"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-23-13","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":23,"verse":13,"english":"Or did your wisdom, wise and good as you were, come to naught? For God, who is the origin of all beings, make (every one) reap the fruit of his own acts.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-32-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6023013","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fb6214e2c8af3317e352b5f59a0e7552d25273e83324ec448a14e00450660edd","compact":"08eb97b14501dc89dbf7add40d7729ca51e0fc20b0787b6720da41b40129752b","nasal":"08eb97b14501dc89dbf7add40d7729ca51e0fc20b0787b6720da41b40129752b"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-23-14","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":23,"verse":14,"english":"And why, versed in polity as you wast, did you come by death, unforeseen? You were acquainted with the means of warding off misfortune, and skilled in doing so.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-32-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6023014","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"67fbcae2caaf12c5dc107f825736d8a062de788d737dae4a23329e8f7c38699e","compact":"3d54d71c1b2c3318d0263baacada76a7b4e7250b574cf542ddc9889e81408210","nasal":"068c1e9a4390da017267c380a93ac72303ffe32c2272aedbc2cb2881e3bc1104"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-23-15","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":23,"verse":15,"english":"Having been brought hither by representing the Fatal Night, fierce and fell, after (being) embraced, and by force, the lotus-eyed one has met with his death. Here lie you, O longarmed one, leaving me lone, and embracing the Earth like your beloved fair.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.867,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-32-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6023015","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"70509bb5564a0d1d35ea68e6ff9d007f01a4e54c40c52d2eef2fbfadfbb94541","compact":"4d8ca2224d76efc9e5442c1db6adeb3cae34580768df6e32f6a3cbc827d4a745","nasal":"4d8ca2224d76efc9e5442c1db6adeb3cae34580768df6e32f6a3cbc827d4a745"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-23-16","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":23,"verse":16,"english":"Having been brought hither by representing the Fatal Night, fierce and fell, after (being) embraced, and by force, the lotus-eyed one has met with his death. Here lie you, O longarmed one, leaving me lone, and embracing the Earth like your beloved fair.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.678,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-32-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6023016","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4627719ee570a657e8df5348a1cf321ea97ed56af2f91035c884a2c24fec9f24","compact":"2254530919d52095b9ead2e45b1febf03a316d3a0ea8db64349fdc564bc29fbb","nasal":"de3dc35bd0590dfe327e20722195f3e116511c8b87c86c1dc1e02bdd559b1477"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-23-17","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":23,"verse":17,"english":"Ever carefully worshipped with perfumed wreaths, this bow of your, O hero, embellished with gold, is dear to me.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.952,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-32-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6023017","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"005c6307b8008afbdbf859fedf463fa1cf33cf4ca2f1077ae16aa373146c983c","compact":"ea28ce12c41301ab37dc04d94ffcb923f901ea1d90149e2fc851b3b7eac16b0f","nasal":"54ea85b56cebd99493f2f614a798b4b17a2c7359e152764a94d5f69a71b1f076"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-23-18","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":23,"verse":18,"english":"O sinless one, you have surely gone to heaven, and (are there) in the company of your sire and my father-in-law, Dasaratha, and all your ancestors.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.852,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-32-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6023018","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8ec3d9f1b3def5349732bd5afb9a37a76a051f35b5717440e2cc24f99049c53c","compact":"a791cb3fe642e49e4c44ec77cd8edeac96a972abc736173b4f99695f1b91a50e","nasal":"a791cb3fe642e49e4c44ec77cd8edeac96a972abc736173b4f99695f1b91a50e"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-23-19","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":23,"verse":19,"english":"You have become a star of the firmament as the fruit of your great act.* You have disregarded your righteous race of Rājarşis. *The carrying out the command of your sire.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.609,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-32-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6023019","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"70bfa04f7a1e9526d3a74056e89327a9a1edf609673fdd082e45485cff793121","compact":"1043d5c9e74173eb9991ae36d82facc50dbbc6bad8866524b7dd4268be638cac","nasal":"34e85d278aa3383594601716874d6b60555d1bc877ec84aa4fccf0e67d8f7c47"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-23-20","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":23,"verse":20,"english":"O king, why do you not look at me? And why is it that you do not answer me, who am a girl, hardly arrived at youth, and who am your wife and companion?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.671,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-32-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6023020","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a86a6476f8b6cf7584c55bba3e4b731ecc03ed69a29c7bed0f75d7304ecd375b","compact":"a5b1e019f624bfb5f9d4bf47c0f346ccc1b1840071022acc85519654bdf0bbde","nasal":"febff3e717c507efa2e71d1fffa4e5cfa39da33866d8862c91ccc7baeb5a0c9c"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-23-21","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":23,"verse":21,"english":"That you at the time of your espousing my hand had vowed, I will practise (righteousness) with you, do you, O Kakutstha, recollect the same, and take me, who am overwhelmed with distrees.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.758,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-32-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6023021","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4acfbe2de6e211c3c3b2ae8469b0d3ed4c719ce08fde0f09ffacbbff9fef8341","compact":"ac681dab7f8c362ed4855dc92ec74e1c30729ac85ade814233808bb9b00d3631","nasal":"ac681dab7f8c362ed4855dc92ec74e1c30729ac85ade814233808bb9b00d3631"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-23-22","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":23,"verse":22,"english":"Why, O best of goers, have you gone from this world to that other, leaving behind me, overwhelmed with distress?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.862,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-32-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6023022","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bfda9ff781f6ff094fcdcea7bd65b726659767b1afe7e189a5dab96ecce400ed","compact":"b7b68e75d13bafac5e2f0dcff1708a6ca8a7375457f6fe255ed15425db3462fc","nasal":"b7b68e75d13bafac5e2f0dcff1708a6ca8a7375457f6fe255ed15425db3462fc"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-23-23","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":23,"verse":23,"english":"That person of your which, decked out with auspicious things, I used to embrace, beasts of prey will for certain tear the same.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.769,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-32-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6023023","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9869c4303cb4feba940ea98db8de19ca1f19160a6ca3e3dfe9eed1aba61762d7","compact":"7c5